# Build context hygiene for `context: "."` image builds (Nx project.json / CI).
# Mirrors the `ignore=` lists in the app Tiltfiles so unrelated churn and the
# multi-GB local target/ dir never enter the context or bust layer caches.
target/
**/target/
.git/
**/.git/
**/node_modules/
**/*.md
# ...except crate READMEs: three crates (`libs/core/strings`,
# `libs/core/proc_macros/{api_resource,sea_orm_resource}`) make their README the
# crate-level rustdoc via `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`, so the file
# is a compile input, not docs churn. Without this negation every Rust image
# build died with `couldn't read libs/core/strings/src/../README.md`.
# Last matching rule wins, so this MUST stay below `**/*.md`.
!**/README.md
**/k8s/
**/Tiltfile
# Host-built N-API addons: node.Dockerfile compiles the `.node` for the image's
# own platform, so the developer's macOS binary must never leak into context.
**/*.node
# NOTE: `dist/` is intentionally NOT globally ignored here.
# Frontend image builds (e.g. zerg-web) need their own dist in context and use a
# per-build `only=[...]` whitelist. Backend (Rust) builds whitelist `apps/`, so
# they carry `**/dist/` in their own `ignore=` to stay isolated from dist churn.
